abstract: >-
  This archive holds the mining-study evidence behind the accompanying paper on the Qiskit
  transpiler's output-equivalence oracle. The study finds that 19 of 68 merged Qiskit
  transpiler bug-fixes (28%, 95% Wilson CI 19-40%), and 29 of 104 in a secondary
  wider-window check (27.9%, CI 20-37%), repair faults that an output-equivalence
  oracle cannot observe by construction: a corrupted layout/permutation record,
  broken fixed-seed determinism, or a dropped global phase, while the compiled
  output stays correct. The same gap replicates in tket (7/21, 33%) and, on a
  smaller exploratory sample, in Cirq (2/10, 20%). The archive includes the frozen
  coding codebook, raw and adjudicated coding labels, cross-SDK replication
  worksheets, surface-characteristic data, and signed coder declarations.
